msgid "Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid "General overview"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Dev UI is a developer-friendly user interface that comes to life "
"when you run your application in development mode (`./mvnw quarkus:dev`).\n"
"It serves as a powerful portal for exploring, debugging, and interacting "
"with your application - all while it's running - with zero code changes or "
"restarts."
msgstr ""

msgid "What is Dev UI?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Dev UI is designed to boost developer joy by making Quarkus' inner "
"workings observable and extensible. It offers:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Insight into available extensions and their capabilities"
msgstr ""

msgid "Access to runtime metadata and tools"
msgstr ""

msgid "A responsive frontend that integrates tightly with hot reload"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A flexible way for extensions to expose configuration, documentation, and "
"actions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether you're a developer exploring your project or an extension author "
"enhancing the experience, Dev UI is your entry point."
msgstr ""

msgid "Layout at a Glance"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When running in dev mode, Quarkus provides a dynamic, modular web interface "
"accessible at http://localhost:8080/q/dev-ui. You can also click `d` in the "
"console log, that will open your default browser at Dev UI."
msgstr ""

msgid "The basic layout has the following parts:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Menu"
msgstr ""

msgid "Page"
msgstr ""

msgid "Footer"
msgstr ""

msgid "Card"
msgstr ""

msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

msgid "Below is a visual overview of the layout:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Menu (Left Sidebar)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The *menu* on the left-hand side provides structured access to built-in "
"pages:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Menu Item"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Extensions*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Displays all Quarkus extensions (used by the current application) as cards. "
"Each card may provide configuration, documentation, or tools."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Configuration*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Shows all configuration options (with current, default, and documentation "
"info). Includes a config editor (text & form modes)."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Workspace*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A project file browser. Files can be opened and edited inline. Extensions "
"may add workspace actions."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Endpoints*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lists all HTTP endpoints (REST, GraphQL, internal, etc.). Helps you inspect "
"available routes in your app."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Continuous Testing*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Monitors and controls continuous testing. View test results, rerun tests, or "
"toggle testing state."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Dev Services*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Displays information about automatically started services (e.g., databases, "
"Kafka brokers)."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Build Metrics*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Provides performance metrics from the last build and reload cycle."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Readme*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders your project's `README.md`, if available. Useful for onboarding or "
"project context."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Dependencies*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Shows all runtime and deployment dependencies with dependency path "
"exploration and search functionality."
msgstr ""

msgid "Page Area (Main Content)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The *main panel* displays content for the selected menu item or extension. "
"Depending on the selected page, it may render:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension-specific tools and UIs (e.g., GraphQL UI, Swagger UI)"
msgstr ""

msgid "JSON viewers, code editors, or metrics charts"
msgstr ""

msgid "Interactive actions (e.g., buttons, toggles)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Documentation and links"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pages are modular and dynamically loaded. Extensions can contribute custom "
"pages written using Web Components and interact with the backend via JSON-"
"RPC."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The *footer* at the bottom is primarily used to display logs while the "
"application runs in dev mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the `Server` log (standard Quarkus log output) is selected, but "
"additional log tabs may appear depending on which extensions are present. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`HTTP`, `GraphQL`,`Scheduler`, etc., may appear when relevant extensions are "
"in use"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`Dev Services` log output from started services like databases, Kafka "
"brokers, etc."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This live log view helps developers track behavior, debug issues, and "
"monitor Dev Services without switching to the terminal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cards"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each Quarkus extension that contributes to Dev UI is represented as a card "
"in the *Extensions* page. These cards provide quick access to features, "
"documentation, configuration, and runtime tools offered by the extension."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each card may include the following elements:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Element"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Logo* _(optional)_"
msgstr ""

msgid "An optional logo representing the extension or its domain"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Title*"
msgstr ""

msgid "The name of the extension as recognized in the Dev UI."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Favorite*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Marks the card as a favorite. Favorited cards are always displayed first in "
"the Extensions view for easier access."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Guide* _(optional)_"
msgstr ""

msgid "Links to the online Quarkus guide for the extension (if available)."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Description*"
msgstr ""

msgid "A short explanation of what the extension does or enables."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Page Links* _(optional)_"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Interactive entries that navigate to custom pages contributed by the "
"extension. A page link can also optionally contain a label that we discuss "
"later."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A shortcut to the configuration editor filtered to settings relevant to this "
"extension."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Underlying Library* _(optional)_"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shows the version of the main library powering the extension (if any)."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Text* _(optional)_"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Displays informational text values (such as versions, counts, or status) as "
"badge-style elements. Can show static, dynamic (fetched once), or streaming "
"(continuously updated) values."
msgstr ""

msgid "*More Details*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Opens a dialog with all information"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions are free to customize their cards and add interactive behaviors "
"based on what they provide at runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid "The settings page is a dialog that contains settings for Dev UI:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Theme (Change between Desktop/Light/Dark"
msgstr ""

msgid "Locale (Change to another supported language/locale)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Bugs / Feature requests"
msgstr ""

msgid "Storage (Manage local browser storage used in Dev UI)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev MCP (Enable your Dev Mode to expose a MCP Server)"
msgstr ""

msgid "... and more... (Other extensions might add to this)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Guide for Extension Developers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus extensions can enhance the developer experience by contributing to "
"the Dev UI. The rest of this guide outlines how to integrate your extension "
"into the Dev UI, covering metadata configuration, adding pages to the card, "
"menu, and footer, and best practices for dynamic content."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-extension.yaml"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To have your extension appear in the Dev UI, ensure the `quarkus-extension."
"yaml` file is present in the `src/main/resources/META-INF` directory of your "
"extension's *runtime* module. This file provides metadata that the Dev UI "
"uses to generate the extension card."
msgstr ""

msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Key fields:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`name`: Displayed as the extension title in the Dev UI card."
msgstr ""

msgid "`description`: Shown as the card's summary."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`guide`: URL to the extension's guide; used to render the guide icon on the "
"card."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`metadata.config`: Filters configuration keys shown when clicking "
"\"Configuration\" on the card."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adding Pages to the Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your extension needs to have the following dependency in it's deployment "
"module:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This can be transitively or directly and is only needed in deployment module."
" This gives your processor access to the relative Build Items."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions can contribute interactive pages to the Dev UI in the following "
"areas:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Card**: Add links to pages directly on the extension card."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Footer**: Add tabs to the footer for logs or other runtime information."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Menu**: Add pages to the Dev UI's left-hand menu."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Settings**: Add a tab to the settings dialog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Unlisted**: Pages that are not listed anywhere above, but are added to the "
"router and can be linked to."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The most common way to contribute to Dev UI is via Pages from your extension "
"card in the Extension page."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add links to your extension's card, produce a `CardPageBuildItem` in a "
"`@BuildStep`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Always make sure that this build step is only run when in local dev mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add anything on the card, you must return/produce a `CardPageBuildItem`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can optionally add a logo (dark and light mode) in `deployment/src/main/"
"resources/dev-ui/`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add a link on the card, you can use the `addPage` method, as all links go "
"to a \"page\". `Page` has some builders to assist with building a page. The "
"most common one is the `webComponentPageBuilder` - but we will discuss some "
"others later."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can (optionally) add the title, else it will be derived from the "
"component link."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add an icon. All free https://fontawesome.com/icons[font-awesome] "
"icons are available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add the link to the web component source (`js`) file in `deployment/src/main/"
"resources/dev-ui/`. This has to take the format of qwc-extensionname-"
"pagename.js"
msgstr ""

msgid "Later we will discuss how to create this web component page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Note about icons"
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional: Library Version"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add an underlying library badge on the card. This is useful for "
"cases where the extension is exposing a well known library. As example, the "
"`quarkus-hibernate-orm` extension provides access to Hibernate. Showing the "
"underlying Hibernate details could be useful information for the user:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This can be done using the `addLibraryVersion` method:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You provide the groupId and artifactId (so that we can look up the version) "
"and a Name and optionally a url."
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional: Build Time Data"
msgstr ""

msgid "You can pass data gathered during build to the Page (js):"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add multiple of these key-value pairs for all the data you know at "
"build time that you need on the page."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The key will be scoped automatically, so you do not have to prefix any "
"namespace. Later we will discuss how to access this data in the webcomponent "
"(page)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional: Labels"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add an optional label to the link in the card using one of the "
"builder methods on the page builder. These labels can be"
msgstr ""

msgid "static (known at build time) `.staticLabel(\"staticLabelValue\")`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"dynamic (loaded at runtime) `."
"dynamicLabelJsonRPCMethodName(\"yourJsonRPCMethodName\")`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"streaming (continuously streaming updated values at runtime) `."
"streamingLabelJsonRPCMethodName(\"yourJsonRPCMethodName\")`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For dynamic and streaming labels, the method name is the name of the JsonRPC "
"method, that we will discuss later."
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional: Card Actions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add action buttons to your extension's card. Unlike page links "
"(which navigate to a page), actions trigger behavior when clicked — they "
"call a JsonRPC method or hit a URL and optionally show the result as a toast "
"notification."
msgstr ""

msgid "To add an action, use the `addAction` method on `CardPageBuildItem`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Create an action using the `CardAction.actionBuilder()` factory."
msgstr ""

msgid "The button label (required)."
msgstr ""

msgid "A Font Awesome icon displayed next to the label (optional)."
msgstr ""

msgid "A tooltip shown on hover (optional)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The JsonRPC method to call when the button is clicked. This uses the same "
"JsonRPC service as page labels — we will discuss how to create JsonRPC "
"services later."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the result of the JsonRPC call is shown as a toast notification. "
"To disable this:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Set to `false` to suppress the result notification."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can also create URL actions that send a GET request to a URL:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `url()` instead of `jsonRpcMethodName()` to hit a URL endpoint."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can combine page links and action buttons on the same card:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional: Card Texts"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can display text values directly on your extension's card. Unlike page "
"links (which navigate to a page) or actions (which trigger behavior), card "
"texts show informational data — such as versions, counts, or status "
"indicators — as badge-style elements on the card itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "Card texts support three modes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Static** — a fixed value known at build time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Dynamic** — a value fetched once at runtime via a JsonRPC method call."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Streaming** — a value continuously updated at runtime via a streaming "
"JsonRPC method."
msgstr ""

msgid "To add a text, use the `addText` method on `CardPageBuildItem`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a card text using the `CardText.textBuilder()` factory."
msgstr ""

msgid "An optional label displayed next to the value."
msgstr ""

msgid "A static text value known at build time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For runtime values fetched once, use `dynamicText` with a JsonRPC method "
"name:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The JsonRPC method to call once to fetch the current value."
msgstr ""

msgid "For continuously updated values, use `streamingText`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The streaming JsonRPC method that pushes updated values."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optional parameters to pass to the streaming method. These are resolved from "
"the extension's local storage."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add multiple card texts, and combine them with page links and "
"actions on the same card."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Apart from adding a card and a page, extensions can add a tab to the footer. "
"This is useful for things that are happening continuously. A page will "
"disconnect from the DOM (and maybe the backend) when navigating away from "
"that page (or webcomponent), and a log in the footer will be permanently "
"connected to the DOM, as it's always part of the view (or app)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are 2 ways to add things to the footer. There easiest is to just "
"expose the log in a BuildItem. Here we expect either a supplier (function) "
"that return a `Flow.Publisher<String>` or a "
"RuntimeValue<SubmissionPublisher<String>>:"
msgstr ""

msgid "You must return/produce a `FooterLogBuildItem`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Here return a Flow.Publisher<String> that will stream the log"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The RuntimeValue is useful if the log is only available at runtime. If you "
"can get the log in the deployment module you can use the supplier."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Or you can take full control of the UI and produce a `FooterPageBuildItem` "
"and provide a custom web component in a js file:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add anything on the footer, you must return/produce a "
"`FooterPageBuildItem`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add a tab in the footer, you can use the `addPage` method, as all tabs "
"renders a \"page\". `Page` has some builders to assist with building a page. "
"The most common one is the `webComponentPageBuilder` - but we will discuss "
"some others later."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can add an icon. All free font-awesome icons are available."
msgstr ""

msgid "To add a page to the Dev UI menu, produce a `MenuPageBuildItem`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add anything on the menu, you must return/produce a `MenuPageBuildItem`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add a link in the menu, you can use the `addPage` method, as all links go "
"to a \"page\". `Page` has some builders to assist with building a page. The "
"most common one is the `webComponentPageBuilder` - but we will discuss some "
"others later."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This page will appear alongside built-in menu items like \"Configuration\" "
"or \"Workspace.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add a tab to the Dev UI settings dialog, produce a `SettingPageBuildItem`:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add anything on the settings tab, you must return/produce a "
"`SettingPageBuildItem`."
msgstr ""

msgid "To add a tab in the setting dialog, you can use the `addPage` method."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This page will be loaded as the content for that tab in the settings dialog"
msgstr ""

msgid "Unlisted Page"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lastly, you can add pages that is not listed anywhere, but added to the "
